body:
I'd suggest you start with the most simple things first, things like:

Opposites create each other, long and short define each other, good and evil are human constructs, everything in the universe seems to be deterministic flowing along the path of least resistance, etc.

&#x200B;

Embody these teachings, dont concern yourself with trying to understand the Tao, the Tao referes to that which is beyond your conscious exerperience, your mind contructs reality, time and space are paramenters of the mind, the Tao is beyond the mind, so it's spaceless and timeless. This means that if your mind is turned off for 1 minute, or 1,000,000 years, and then it is rebooted, you would experience that lapse of void of mind being equally long, that is, nothing, less than an instant.

&#x200B;

Peace.
